Subject: [PATCH] XR: PPE bridge templates must not decrement the IP TTL

AP37 bounded trial 1 captured TTL 64 forwarded as 63 once bridge subflows were
bound (software bridge kept 64). Bridge templates no longer set
AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_TTL; routed flow types keep it. L2 subflows inherit the
template ib1 except packet type and UDP, so the bit is gone for them too.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -471,8 +471,13 @@
 	      FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_UDP, l4proto == IPPROTO_UDP) |
 	      FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_VLAN_LAYER, data->vlan.num) |
 	      FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_VPM, data->vlan.num) |
-	      FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_PPPOE, data->pppoe.num) |
-	      AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_TTL;
+	      FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_PPPOE, data->pppoe.num);
+	/* A bridge never changes the IP TTL. AP37 trial 1 measured bound bridge
+	 * subflows forwarding TTL 64 as 63 with this bit set; L2 subflows inherit
+	 * every ib1 bit except packet type/UDP from this template.
+	 */
+	if (type != PPE_PKT_TYPE_BRIDGE)
+		val |= AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_TTL;
 	hwe->ib1 = val;
 
 	val = FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB2_PORT_AG, 0x1f);
